doi: "10.5281/zenodo.14982104"
abstract: >
  SAGE is an open-source evaluation framework and live observability platform
  that measures security boundary drift (vulnerability injection rate), specification
  gaming (proxy gap), capability gain, and catastrophic forgetting in self-modifying
  autonomous code agents across iterative evolutionary cycles. Evaluated across 35
  runs and 9,800 canonical task executions on Kaggle Dual Tesla T4 GPUs across seven
  agent archetypes (G1-G7).
keywords:
  - autonomous agents
  - self-evolving code agents
  - security boundary drift
  - benchmark
  - LLM evaluation
  - reinforcement learning
  - capability retention
  - reward hacking
